      "id": "photography-tajhat-zamindar-bari",
      "title": "Tajhat Zamindar Bari",
      "description": "Photo Essay: Tajhat Zamindar Bari\n\nLocated approximately three kilometres southeast of Rangpur city, Tajhat Zamindar Bari is one of the country's most remarkable architectural and archaeological heritage sites. The palace was built in the early 20th century by Maharaja Gopal Lal Roy, a professional jeweller. It is believed that the estate derived its name, 'Tajhat', from the magnificent crown (Taj) he once wore.\n\nFrom 1984 to 1991, the palace served as a branch of the Bangladesh Supreme Court. It was declared a protected monument by the Department of Archaeology in 1995 and now houses the Rangpur Museum.",
